{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe `scanner-integration (pinned Semgrep + Gitleaks on the patchset)` job, added to `main` in\n`6125c5345f01` (Gerrit 2595, ticket aa9e), casts `Verified -1` on effectively every change pushed\nsince it merged, blocking all merges.\n\n**Root fault (Defect 1), quoted from a real job log** (branch-head lane, run 33834183836 job\n100903189596, a tree that carries the scanner script):\n\n```\nreview scanner locks: OK\n/bin/sh: 1: set: Illegal option -o pipefail\nmake: *** [Makefile: scanner-integration] Error 2\n```\n\nThe `scanner-integration` recipe opens with `@set -euo pipefail;`. The Makefile sets no `SHELL`, so\nGNU make runs the recipe under `/bin/sh` — dash on ubuntu-latest, which has no `pipefail`.\n`set -o pipefail` is a dash **runtime** error at the `set` builtin (NOT a parse error — `dash -n`\ndoes not validate `set` option arguments). The recipe body contains no pipeline, so `pipefail` is\ninert.\n\n**Exact location (current tree, rebased on Gerrit 2600, which shifted Makefile line numbers):** the\n`scanner-integration` recipe header is at **Makefile:499** and the offending `@set -euo pipefail;`\nis at **Makefile:500**. (The quoted log's `Makefile:475` reflects the pre-2600 revision; the line\nhas since moved to 500.)\n\n**How it landed broken.** 2595's own Verified run 33831682168 contains 26 jobs and NO\n`scanner-integration` job at all: the Verified lane runs `gerrit-verify.yaml` from trusted `main`,\nwhich did not yet wire the lane, so 2595's `+1` was cast without the new job ever executing.\n\n## Approach\n\nReplace `set -euo pipefail` with POSIX `set -eu` in the `scanner-integration` recipe (Makefile:500).\nThe recipe has no pipeline, so this is behaviour-preserving under bash and correct under dash. It is\na one-line change and introduces no new script, config key, env var, feature flag, or lock, so the\nmechanism-delta ratchet sees nothing new.\n\nStacked on Gerrit 2600 so this change's OWN Verified run exercises the (now-fixed)\n`scanner-integration` job on a tree that carries the scanner script — so, unlike 2595, this change\nis validated by the very job it repairs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `Makefile` — the `scanner-integration` recipe's `set` line (Makefile:500) only.\n\n## Deferred to follow-up b973-b298-9b5d-4765 (discovered_from this ticket)\n\nIntentionally OUT of scope for this incident fix:\n- Defect 2: `_scanner-integration.yml` lacks the `[ -f scripts/install_review_scanners.py ]`\n  predates-gate guard, so a change based before `6125c534` fails `No such file` until rebased.\n- The vacuous-vote escape closure: derive `test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`'s guarded set from\n  the `gerrit-verify.yaml`/`test.yml` local-`uses:` closure, plus a STATIC bash-only-construct scan\n  over CI-reachable make recipes (a parse-only `dash -n` check does not catch `set -o pipefail`).\n\n## Testing\n\n- Defect-seeded RED/GREEN (executable, portable, no CI provider required): `sh -c 'set -euo pipefail'`\n  exits nonzero with `Illegal option -o pipefail` — the exact production failure — while\n  `sh -c 'set -eu'` exits 0. Verified locally under dash. (Executing the leading `set` line under\n  dash is a valid detection oracle; a parse-only check is not.)\n- No-pipeline check: the recipe body (Makefile:500-506) contains no `|`, confirming `pipefail` was\n  inert and the change is behaviour-preserving.\n- Integration proof: this change's own `scanner-integration` Verified job reaches `+1` (green),\n  where it was `-1` on every change before the fix.\n- Verification set: `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The `scanner-integration` recipe at Makefile:500 reads `@set -eu;` (was `@set -euo pipefail;`);\n      the citation matches the actual recipe location (header Makefile:499). Checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] Defect-seeded RED/GREEN recorded: `sh -c 'set -euo pipefail'` fails with `Illegal option -o\n      pipefail` and `sh -c 'set -eu'` succeeds. Checked by the quoted shell output in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] The `scanner-integration` Verified job passes on this change (was red on every change since\n      `6125c534`). Checked by this change reaching `Verified +1` with the `scanner-integration` job green.\n- [ ] No new mechanism is introduced (no script/config/env/flag/lock). Checked by the mechanism-delta\n      ratchet staying green in `make lint`.\n- [ ] The two deferred hardening items are captured in linked follow-up b973-b298-9b5d-4765. Checked\n      by the `discovered_from` link."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788501453366396900,"uuid":"81924d86-1f6c-47e4-a04e-32e0af561848"}